# ClawQL environment variables — `.env.example`
#
# Index (sections below):
#   1. API spec selection          7. MCP transport + HTTP health/metrics
#   2. Native GraphQL / gRPC       8. Feature tiers (quick reference)
#   3. dotenv + CLAWQL_* names     9. Memory, vault, PageIndex, auth
#   4. Upstream API auth           10. Optional MCP tools (notify, workflow, …)
#   5. Document / IDP vendors      11. Sandbox
#   6. fetch-provider-specs        12. Dashboard / OpenClaw bridge
#
# Convention: **`CLAWQL_ENABLE_*=1`** opt in · **`=0`** opt out · unset = default for that flag.
# Core tools (`search`, `execute`, `audit`, `cache`) have no enable flag.
# Full guide: docs/readme/configuration.md

# ─── 1. API spec selection ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Two stages (same story as README "Configure the API spec"):
#
# Stage 1 — Multi-spec merge (merged operation index), if any applies:
#   1) CLAWQL_SPEC_PATHS
#   2) CLAWQL_BUNDLED_PROVIDERS = comma-separated ids from BUNDLED_PROVIDERS + optional "google" (GCP manifest)
#   3) CLAWQL_PROVIDER = merged preset (google, all-providers, atlassian, …)
#   4) Else if nothing selected multi and PATH / URL / DISCOVERY unset → all-providers (default)
#
# Stage 2 — Single spec (if Stage 1 does not apply), first match wins:
#   CLAWQL_SPEC_PATH > CLAWQL_SPEC_URL > CLAWQL_DISCOVERY_URL > CLAWQL_PROVIDER (single vendor)

# Multi-spec mode (one process, merged operation index)
# - List local spec files (comma, semicolon, or newline separated):
# CLAWQL_SPEC_PATHS=providers/google/apis/compute-v1/discovery.json,providers/google/apis/container-v1/discovery.json
# - Or merge bundled vendors by id (plus optional "google" = full GCP on-disk set):
# CLAWQL_BUNDLED_PROVIDERS=github,cloudflare,slack,n8n

# Single explicit spec (OpenAPI / Discovery)
# CLAWQL_SPEC_PATH=./openapi.yaml
# CLAWQL_SPEC_URL=https://petstore3.swagger.io/api/v3/openapi.json
# (Relative servers[].url is resolved against this document URL; CLAWQL_API_BASE_URL overrides.)
# CLAWQL_DISCOVERY_URL=https://run.googleapis.com/$discovery/rest?version=v2

# Bundled preset (used when explicit spec vars above are not set)
# Single specs: atlassian | cloudflare | github | slack | sentry | n8n | tika | gotenberg | paperless | stirling | onyx
# Merged presets: google | all-providers | atlassian
# all-providers = Google Cloud (bundled) + every other bundled vendor (jira, bitbucket, cloudflare, …)
# CLAWQL_PROVIDER=google

# Optional: fail fast if bundled local file is missing (never fetch fallback URL)
# CLAWQL_BUNDLED_OFFLINE=1

# Base URL for REST calls (overrides servers[0].url in the spec if set).
# CLAWQL_API_BASE_URL=https://api.example.com

# ─── 2. Custom provider endpoints (advanced — prefer CLAWQL_PROVIDER for bundled vendors) ───
# Most users only need CLAWQL_PROVIDER (e.g. linear, github, cloudflare). ClawQL picks the best
# internal connection per provider (gRPC → GraphQL → OpenAPI). You only need search + execute.
#
# Linear (recommended):
#   CLAWQL_PROVIDER=linear
#   LINEAR_API_KEY=lin_api_...
#
# Custom GraphQL HTTP API (not in the bundled catalog):
#   CLAWQL_GRAPHQL_URL=https://api.example.com/graphql
#   CLAWQL_GRAPHQL_NAME=myapi
#   CLAWQL_GRAPHQL_HEADERS={"Authorization":"Bearer …"}
# When upstream blocks introspection, optional on-disk index files (execute still POSTs to the URL):
#   CLAWQL_GRAPHQL_SCHEMA_PATH=./schemas/vendor.graphql
#   CLAWQL_GRAPHQL_INTROSPECTION_PATH=./schemas/vendor-introspection.json
#
# Multiple custom endpoints: JSON array (merged with CLAWQL_GRAPHQL_URL when both set).
# Missing schemaPath/introspectionPath files are logged and ignored; HTTP introspection is tried.
# Known endpoints (e.g. api.linear.app/graphql) auto-route to bundled providers when available.
# CLAWQL_GRAPHQL_SOURCES=[{"name":"myapi","endpoint":"https://api.example.com/graphql","headers":{"Authorization":"Bearer …"},"schemaPath":"./schemas/myapi.graphql"}]
#
# Custom gRPC service:
# CLAWQL_GRPC_SOURCES=[{"name":"svc","endpoint":"127.0.0.1:50051","protoPath":"./proto/helloworld.proto","insecure":true}]

# ─── 3. dotenv loading + canonical CLAWQL_* names ───────────────────────
# Entrypoints import load-env: package-root .env first, then cwd .env (cwd wins on duplicate keys).
# Prefer CLAWQL_* everywhere; OPENAPI_* / GOOGLE_DISCOVERY_URL remain aliases for spec selection only.
# Details: docs/readme/configuration.md § ".env loading and canonical CLAWQL_* names"

# ─── 4. Upstream API auth (execute / GraphQL proxy) ─────────────────────
# Local Docker Desktop k8s: `bash scripts/kubernetes/k8s-docker-desktop-set-mcp-auth.sh` syncs these into Secret `clawql-github-auth` on `deployment/clawql-mcp-http` (optional `.env`; see docker/README.md).
# Multi-spec default: set tokens for each vendor you call (see src/auth-headers.ts and README).
# Option A — one JSON object, keys = merged specLabel (github, cloudflare, slack, compute-v1, …).
# Use "google" as catch-all for all Google Cloud Discovery slugs unless you set a slug-specific key.
# Use "aws" as catch-all for optional extra headers on AWS slugs (SigV4 uses AWS_* env vars, not Bearer).
# Values: bare string → Authorization: Bearer …, or {"Authorization":"Token …","X-Custom":"1"}.
# CLAWQL_PROVIDER_AUTH_JSON={"github":"ghp_…","cloudflare":"…","google":"ya29.…","slack":"xoxb-…","paperless":"…"}
# Option B — per-vendor env vars (merged with Option A; map entries win on conflict):
# CLAWQL_GOOGLE_ACCESS_TOKEN=…   # or GOOGLE_ACCESS_TOKEN (e.g. gcloud auth print-access-token)
# AWS SigV4 (bundled `aws` preset / slugs like ec2-2016-11-15) — required for live execute:
# AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=…
# AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=…
# AWS_SESSION_TOKEN=…              # optional (STS / assumed role)
# AWS_REGION=us-east-1             # or CLAWQL_AWS_REGION / AWS_DEFAULT_REGION
# CLAWQL_CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=…
# Cloudflare Global API Key (alternative to API token): account email + key from the dashboard (sends X-Auth-Email / X-Auth-Key).
# CLOUDFLARE_EMAIL=…
# CLOUDFLARE_API_KEY=…
# CLAWQL_GITHUB_TOKEN=ghp_…
# Kubernetes local (`make local-k8s-up`): ClawQL GHCR images are **public** by default (docker-publish verifies anonymous reads).
# Only if your fork keeps packages private: set a read:packages PAT so a **kyverno** docker-registry Secret is created and wired
# into the Cosign ClusterPolicy (CLAWQL_KYVERNO_GHCR_PULL_TOKEN preferred; else GITHUB_TOKEN / GH_TOKEN / CLAWQL_GITHUB_TOKEN).
# CLAWQL_KYVERNO_GHCR_PULL_TOKEN=ghp_…
# CLAWQL_GHCR_PULL_USERNAME=your-github-login
# Linear GraphQL (bundled provider `linear` — merged specLabel `linear`): raw API key in Authorization (no Bearer prefix)
# LINEAR_API_KEY=lin_api_…
# Notion REST (bundled provider `notion` — merged specLabel `notion`): integration secret + required API version header
# NOTION_API_TOKEN=secret_…
# NOTION_VERSION=2022-06-28
# Optional fallback for other merged vendors or single-vendor mode:
# CLAWQL_BEARER_TOKEN=…
# Global extra headers (X-*, etc.). If CLAWQL_PROVIDER_AUTH_JSON is unset, Authorization here applies to every call.
# CLAWQL_HTTP_HEADERS={"X-Trace-Id":"…"}

# ─── 5. Self-hosted document stack (merged specLabel base URLs) ─────────
# PAPERLESS_BASE_URL=http://paperless:8000
# PAPERLESS_API_TOKEN=…   # charts/clawql-mcp values-docker-desktop default: clawql-local-paperless-dev (doc-pipeline Secret). Fetch script can read that Secret via kubectl when unset and host is paperless.localhost.
# Stirling-PDF — base URL must be reachable from *wherever* the process runs:
# - clawql-mcp / MCP pod in the same namespace as the Helm chart: in-cluster DNS, e.g.
#   STIRLING_BASE_URL=http://clawql-mcp-http-stirling:8080
# - Laptop running `npm run fetch-provider-specs`: NOT ClusterIP. Either:
#   (a) kubectl port-forward -n clawql svc/clawql-mcp-http-stirling 8080:8080  →  STIRLING_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8080
#   (b) Helm providerIngress for stirling enabled →  STIRLING_BASE_URL=http://stirling.localhost  (nginx → service:8080)
# STIRLING_API_KEY=…   # must match Stirling SECURITY_CUSTOMGLOBALAPIKEY / chart documentPipeline.stirling.auth.apiKey
# Optional: comma-separated OpenAPI paths (default `/v1/api-docs,/v3/api-docs` — upstream Stirling uses /v1 per springdoc.api-docs.path)
# STIRLING_OPENAPI_PATHS=/v1/api-docs
# TIKA_BASE_URL=http://tika:9998
# Docling Serve v1 — layout-aware parse (optional sidecar). Auth: DOCLING_API_KEY → X-Api-Key
# DOCLING_BASE_URL=http://localhost:5001
# DOCLING_API_KEY=
# GOTENBERG_BASE_URL=http://gotenberg:3000
# Optional: when Gotenberg does not serve /openapi.json, fetch-provider-specs downloads this YAML (default: Gotenberg v7.10.0 docs/openapi.yaml)
# GOTENBERG_OPENAPI_PIN_URL=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/gotenberg/gotenberg/v7.10.0/docs/openapi.yaml
# Onyx API root (often ends with /api). Auth: ONYX_API_TOKEN (Bearer) for merged specLabel `onyx`.
# ONYX_BASE_URL=http://onyx:8080/api
# ONYX_API_TOKEN=…
# Nextcloud (IDP storage — WebDAV + OCS). Basic auth with app password.
# NEXTCLOUD_BASE_URL=http://nextcloud:8080
# NEXTCLOUD_USERNAME=admin
# NEXTCLOUD_APP_PASSWORD=…
# CLAWQL_ENABLE_NEXTCLOUD_WEBHOOK=1   # POST /idp/nextcloud/webhook → NATS inbox.arrived
# CLAWQL_NEXTCLOUD_WEBHOOK_TOKEN=…   # required in production
# ConeShare (secure sharing / VDR). JWT from `coneshare_token_create` or admin token.
# CONESHARE_BASE_URL=http://coneshare:80
# CONESHARE_API_TOKEN=…
# CLAWQL_ENABLE_CONESHARE=1
# CLAWQL_CONESHARE_WEBHOOK_TOKEN=…   # POST /idp/coneshare/webhook on MCP HTTP server
# CLAWQL_CONESHARE_WEBHOOK_RESUME_WORKFLOW=0  # sync Argo resume from clawql_share
# CLAWQL_CONESHARE_NOTIFY_CHANNEL=C01234567   # optional Slack for NATS follow-up consumer
# IDP automated pipeline runner ([#307](https://github.com/danielsmithdevelopment/ClawQL/issues/307))
# CLAWQL_ENABLE_IDP_PIPELINE=1
# CLAWQL_IDP_REDACT_LIST=SSN,EIN
# CLAWQL_IDP_REQUIRE_STIRLING_REDACT=0
# CLAWQL_IDP_PIPELINE_RUN_TOKEN=…   # Bearer for POST /idp/pipeline/run (NATS workers)
# CLAWQL_MCP_INTERNAL_URL=http://clawql-mcp-http:8080
# CLAWQL_ENABLE_IDP_CLASSIFIER=1
# CLAWQL_ENABLE_LANGEXTRACT=1
# CLAWQL_ENABLE_PDF_INSPECTOR=1
# CLAWQL_ENABLE_ANYDOC=1
# CLASSIFIER_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080
# LANGEXTRACT_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8090
# LANGEXTRACT_MODEL_ID=deepseek/deepseek-chat
# LANGEXTRACT_BACKEND=openrouter
# CLAWQL_PDF_INSPECTOR_FILE_ROOTS=/vault:/fixtures
# CLAWQL_ANYDOC_FILE_ROOTS=/vault:/fixtures
# CLAWQL_PDF_INSPECTOR_LOCAL_MIN_CONFIDENCE=0.85
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=   # live openrouter backend — same key as OpenClaw; never commit
# OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434
# LANGEXTRACT_MODE=demo   # sidecar: demo (default) or live
# CLASSIFIER_MIN_CONFIDENCE=0.85
# IDP_DOCUMENT_URL=https://example.com/idp/inbox/document.pdf
# CLAWQL_IDP_PIPELINE_MAX_RETRIES=2
# CLAWQL_IDP_PIPELINE_RETRY_DELAY_MS=500
# ─── 6. fetch-provider-specs (optional spec refresh) ───────────────────
# (Onyx: same ONYX_BASE_URL + optional ONYX_API_TOKEN for Bearer when pulling /openapi.json)
# `npm run fetch-provider-specs` loads **repo-root `.env`** then **`.env.local`** (override) before reading URLs — no manual `export` needed.
# If a self-hosted base URL is still unset, it defaults to **http://*.localhost** (see charts/clawql-mcp values-docker-desktop).
# Opt out: **`CLAWQL_FETCH_PROVIDER_SPECS_SKIP_SELF_HOSTED=1`** (only public TARGETS fetches) or **`CLAWQL_FETCH_PROVIDER_SPECS_LOCALHOST_DEFAULTS=0`** (no localhost fallbacks).
# If stirling.localhost cannot serve OpenAPI JSON on the tried paths, the fetch script runs **kubectl run … curl** to the Stirling Service (needs kubectl + cluster context). Disable with **`CLAWQL_FETCH_STIRLING_K8S_FALLBACK=0`**.
# Override defaults: **`CLAWQL_FETCH_K8S_NAMESPACE`**, **`CLAWQL_FETCH_STIRLING_K8S_SERVICE`**, **`CLAWQL_FETCH_STIRLING_K8S_SECRET_NAME`** (default secret `…-doc-pipeline-auth`, key `stirling-api-key`), **`CLAWQL_FETCH_STIRLING_K8S_PORT`**.
# Paperless in-cluster fallback: **`CLAWQL_FETCH_PAPERLESS_K8S_SERVICE`**, **`CLAWQL_FETCH_PAPERLESS_K8S_PORT`** (default `clawql-mcp-http-paperless`, `8000`). Disable Secret + in-cluster curl with **`CLAWQL_FETCH_PAPERLESS_K8S_TOKEN=0`**.

# ─── 7. MCP transport, health, metrics, observability ──────────────────
# Stdio entrypoint:   npm start
# HTTP entrypoint:    npm run start:http
# PORT=8080
# MCP_PORT=8080
# MCP_PATH=/mcp
#
# Client / workflow URL (NOT read by clawql-mcp — use Cursor mcp.json "url" or scripts below):
# Tailscale MagicDNS example: CLAWQL_MCP_URL=https://clawql-host.your-tailnet.ts.net/mcp
# Headscale MagicDNS (*.clawql.local) example: CLAWQL_MCP_URL=http://mac-mini.clawql.local:8080/mcp
# npm run workflow:complex-release-stack:mcp uses CLAWQL_MCP_URL to connect to an existing HTTP server.
# Private tailnet: beginner guide docs/deployment/tailscale-and-headscale-for-clawql.md (website /tailscale); docs/readme/deployment.md § "Private tailnet"; Headscale runbook docs/deployment/headscale-tailnet.md (#206); ACL starter docs/deployment/headscale-acls-clawql.hujson (#213)

# Optional: Streamable HTTP GET /healthz includes merkleSnapshot + cuckooMembershipArtifactsEnabled when vault + memory.db flags match (not for default fast probes).
# CLAWQL_HEALTHZ_MEMORY_ARTIFACTS=1

# Optional: GET /healthz includes nativeProtocolMetrics: aggregates + graphqlBySource / grpcBySource (per sourceLabel).
# CLAWQL_HEALTHZ_NATIVE_PROTOCOL_METRICS=1

# GET /metrics — OpenMetrics (prom-client). Default on; opt out:
# CLAWQL_ENABLE_HTTP_METRICS=0

# Observability (see docs/observability/README.md; ADR 0005 planned for 7.0 bundled profile):
# CLAWQL_OBSERVABILITY_PROFILE=external   # bundled | external | minimal
# CLAWQL_ENABLE_OTEL_TRACING=1
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://otel-collector:4318
# OTEL_SERVICE_NAME=clawql-mcp
# CLAWQL_LOKI_PUSH_URL=https://loki.example.com/loki/api/v1/push
# CLAWQL_ENABLE_LOKI_PUSH=0              # opt out when URL is set (default on)
# CLAWQL_LOKI_BEARER_TOKEN=...
# CLAWQL_LOKI_TENANT_ID=...
# CLAWQL_LOKI_JOB=clawql-audit
# CLAWQL_ENABLE_LANGFUSE=0              # work-trace export; default on in bundled profile (when wired)
# LANGFUSE_HOST=https://langfuse.example.com
# LANGFUSE_PUBLIC_KEY=pk-lf-...
# LANGFUSE_SECRET_KEY=sk-lf-...

# OpenAPI→GraphQL runs in-process; Streamable HTTP also serves /graphql.
# Optional: CLAWQL_INTROSPECTION_PATH=./introspection.json

# Browser / Gallery skill: set to * (or a specific origin) so CORS allows fetch + mcp-session-id.
# CLAWQL_CORS_ALLOW_ORIGIN=*

# Optional: gRPC alongside Streamable HTTP (same process as clawql-mcp-http). See README.
# Services: grpc.health.v1.Health, model_context_protocol.Mcp (protobuf; health Check service name: model_context_protocol.Mcp), mcp.transport.v1.Mcp.Session (JSON-RPC; health: mcp.transport.v1.Mcp).
# ENABLE_GRPC=1
# GRPC_MAX_MESSAGE_LENGTH=67108864
# GRPC_PORT=50051
# CLAWQL_MCP_GRPC_ADDR=127.0.0.1:50051
# CLAWQL_MCP_TRANSPORT=grpc
# GRPC_BIND=0.0.0.0
# TLS (optional): mTLS when GRPC_TLS_REQUIRE_CLIENT_CERT=1 and GRPC_TLS_CA_PATH is set.
# GRPC_TLS_CERT_PATH=/path/to/server.crt
# GRPC_TLS_KEY_PATH=/path/to/server.key
# GRPC_TLS_CA_PATH=/path/to/ca.crt
# grpc.health.v1.Health/Check is the standard probe; use grpcurl for smoke tests.
# Optional server reflection (grpcurl list/describe) — off by default for production.
# ENABLE_GRPC_REFLECTION=1

# Optional: pregenerated introspection JSON (skips live introspection for execute field names).
# CLAWQL_INTROSPECTION_PATH=./introspection.json

# ─── 8. Feature tiers (quick reference) ───────────────────────────────
# Canonical: docs/readme/configuration.md § "Feature tiers"
# Always on: search, execute, audit, cache
# Default on, opt out (=0): MEMORY, DOCUMENTS, PAGEINDEX, CLOUDFLARE, HTTP_METRICS
# Default off, opt in (=1): SANDBOX, SCHEDULE, NOTIFY, ONYX, OUROBOROS, OTEL_TRACING (until bundled profile)

# ─── 9. Obsidian vault (memory tools) ───────────────────────────────────
# memory_ingest / memory_recall default ON. Set CLAWQL_ENABLE_MEMORY=0 to hide the tools.
# When CLAWQL_OBSIDIAN_VAULT_PATH is set, the server checks the path is readable/writable at startup.
# Docker images default to /vault (see docker/Dockerfile). Omit locally to skip the check.
# CLAWQL_OBSIDIAN_VAULT_PATH=/vault
# CLAWQL_ENABLE_MEMORY=0

# PageIndex (vectorless hierarchical recall) — default ON; set CLAWQL_ENABLE_PAGEINDEX=0 to hide pageindex_* tools.
# CLAWQL_ENABLE_PAGEINDEX=0
# CLAWQL_PAGEINDEX_PATH=/path/to/vault-or-data

# Code graph (structural AST indexing, Graphify-style) — default OFF; set CLAWQL_ENABLE_CODEGRAPH=1 to register codegraph_* tools.
# CLAWQL_ENABLE_CODEGRAPH=1
# CLAWQL_CODEGRAPH_ROOT=/path/to/repo
# CLAWQL_CODEGRAPH_PATH=/path/to/data
# CLAWQL_CODEGRAPH_MAX_FILES=5000
# CLAWQL_CODEGRAPH_ID=myrepo-codegraph
# Backend: native (default) or graphify (read Graphify graph.json)
# CLAWQL_CODEGRAPH_BACKEND=native
# CLAWQL_CODEGRAPH_GRAPHIFY_JSON=/path/to/graphify-out/graph.json
# Optional: shell command to refresh graph.json before load (e.g. graphify .)
# CLAWQL_CODEGRAPH_GRAPHIFY_REFRESH_CMD=graphify /path/to/repo
# Optional: delegate codegraph_query to Graphify HTTP MCP (python -m graphify.serve graph.json --transport http)
# CLAWQL_CODEGRAPH_GRAPHIFY_MCP_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8080/mcp
# Hybrid memory_recall: merge vault hits with code graph symbols
# CLAWQL_MEMORY_RECALL_HYBRID_CODEGRAPH=1
# CLAWQL_MEMORY_RECALL_CODEGRAPH_LIMIT=8
# CLAWQL_MEMORY_RECALL_HYBRID_PAGEINDEX=1
# CLAWQL_MEMORY_RECALL_PAGEINDEX_LIMIT=8
# CLAWQL_MEMORY_RECALL_HYBRID_ONYX=1
# CLAWQL_MEMORY_RECALL_ONYX_LIMIT=8
# After memory_ingest, rebuild PageIndex for the written note:
# CLAWQL_MEMORY_INGEST_REBUILD_PAGEINDEX=1

# Gateway auth (clawql-auth) — HTTP MCP only. Default noAuth for local dev.
# ClawQL is not an IdP — oidc mode verifies customer-issued JWTs.
# CLAWQL_AUTH_MODE=apiKey
# CLAWQL_API_KEY=your-secret
# CLAWQL_AUTH_MODE=oidc
# CLAWQL_AUTH_OIDC_JWKS_URL=https://idp.example.com/.well-known/jwks.json
# CLAWQL_AUTH_OIDC_ISSUER=https://idp.example.com
# CLAWQL_AUTH_OIDC_AUDIENCE=clawql-mcp
# CLAWQL_AUTH_REQUIRE_MFA_FOR_FINANCIAL=1
# Docs: docs/security/clawql-auth-oidc-stepup.md

# Presidio PII redaction — opt-in; requires analyzer + anonymizer HTTP services.
# CLAWQL_ENABLE_PRESIDIO=1
# CLAWQL_PRESIDIO_ANALYZER_URL=http://127.0.0.1:5001
# CLAWQL_PRESIDIO_ANONYMIZER_URL=http://127.0.0.1:5002
# CLAWQL_PRESIDIO_FAILURE_POLICY=block

# Local Privacy Filter — opt-in backup after Presidio ([#245]). No OpenAI API; local sidecar only.
# CLAWQL_ENABLE_PRIVACY_FILTER=1
# CLAWQL_PRIVACY_FILTER_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8091
# CLAWQL_PRIVACY_FILTER_FAILURE_POLICY=warn
# CLAWQL_PRIVACY_FILTER_MODEL=openai/privacy-filter

# memory_ingest: load `toolOutputs` from a server path (huge files without large MCP tool JSON)
# Unset = allow. Set to 0 / false / off to disable `toolOutputsFile` reads.
# CLAWQL_MEMORY_INGEST_FILE=0
# Comma-separated absolute directory prefixes the file must live under (default: process cwd, realpath).
# CLAWQL_MEMORY_INGEST_FILE_ROOTS=/path/to/ClawQL
# CLAWQL_MEMORY_INGEST_FILE_MAX_BYTES=10000000

# Team vault sync (clawql sync push|pull) — R2 default; S3/GCS via S3-compatible API. See docs/getting-started/team-vault-sync.md
# Config file: ~/.ClawQL/sync.json (bucket + prefix only — no secrets)
# CLAWQL_SYNC_PROVIDER=r2          # r2 (default) | s3 | gcs (aliases: aws, gcp, google)
# CLAWQL_SYNC_BUCKET=acme-clawql-team
# CLAWQL_SYNC_PREFIX=teams/engineering/
# R2:
# CLAWQL_R2_ACCOUNT_ID=
# CLAWQL_SYNC_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# CLAWQL_SYNC_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# S3:
# CLAWQL_AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# CLAWQL_AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# CLAWQL_AWS_REGION=us-east-1
# GCS (S3-compatible HMAC interop — Cloud Storage → Settings → Interoperability):
# CLAWQL_GCS_HMAC_ACCESS_ID=
# CLAWQL_GCS_HMAC_SECRET=
# CLAWQL_SYNC_ENDPOINT=   # override (GCS default: https://storage.googleapis.com)
# CLAWQL_SYNC_REGION=auto

# Auto sync (after memory_ingest / before memory_recall)
# CLAWQL_SYNC_AUTO=1                  # auto-push after successful memory_ingest
# CLAWQL_SYNC_AUTO_DEBOUNCE_MS=2000   # quiet period to coalesce note+index writes (default 2s)
# CLAWQL_SYNC_AUTO_PUSH_MIN_MS=30000  # min gap between pushes while ingesting steadily (default 30s); shutdown flush bypasses this
# CLAWQL_SYNC_AUTO_PULL=1             # throttled pull before memory_recall
# CLAWQL_SYNC_AUTO_PULL_MIN_MS=60000
# CLAWQL_SYNC_AUTO_PULL_ON_START=1    # pull once at MCP startup

# Document stack: bundled tika, gotenberg, paperless, stirling, onyx, nextcloud, coneshare in all-providers; ingest + Onyx tool. Set 0 to opt out.
# CLAWQL_ENABLE_DOCUMENTS=0

# Cloud provider bundles — add-ons for the default install stack (not all-providers).
# Default stack: Cloudflare, GitHub, Slack, Linear, Notion, Onyx.
# CLAWQL_ENABLE_GOOGLE=1
# CLAWQL_ENABLE_CLOUDFLARE=0   # omit Cloudflare from default stack only
# CLAWQL_ENABLE_AWS=1

# ingest_external_knowledge — Markdown bulk + optional URL fetch (issue #40)
# CLAWQL_EXTERNAL_INGEST=1
# CLAWQL_EXTERNAL_INGEST_FETCH=1   # allow HTTPS fetch (url mode); http only for localhost

# ─── 10. Optional MCP tools ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Enterprise audit ring buffer — always registered; tune buffer size only:
# CLAWQL_AUDIT_MAX_ENTRIES=500
# (Loki push env vars are in §7 Observability above)

# Ephemeral in-process KV cache — always registered; LRU; not persisted
# CLAWQL_CACHE_MAX_VALUE_BYTES=1048576
# CLAWQL_CACHE_MAX_ENTRIES=10000

# Slack notify (issue #77)
# CLAWQL_ENABLE_NOTIFY=1
# Test-only (Vitest): avoid real Slack when CLAWQL_TEST_SLACK_FETCH_STUB=1; optional CLAWQL_TEST_SLACK_FETCH_BODY (JSON text), CLAWQL_TEST_SLACK_FETCH_HTTP_OK=0 for HTTP failure path
# CLAWQL_TEST_SLACK_FETCH_STUB=1
# CLAWQL_TEST_SLACK_FETCH_BODY={"ok":true,"channel":"C01234567","ts":"1700000000.000100","message":{"text":"stub"}}
# CLAWQL_TEST_SLACK_FETCH_HTTP_OK=0

# Argo Workflows `workflow` tool (issue #243) — template-ref submit only; requires Argo Workflows >= 3.4.0
# CLAWQL_ENABLE_WORKFLOW=1
# CLAWQL_WORKFLOW_NAMESPACE_ALLOWLIST=clawql,pipelines
# CLAWQL_WORKFLOW_DEFAULT_NAMESPACE=clawql
# CLAWQL_WORKFLOW_KUBECONFIG=/path/to/kubeconfig
# CLAWQL_WORKFLOW_TEMPLATE_ALLOWLIST=clawql/clawql-vault-daily-digest
# CLAWQL_WORKFLOW_ARGO_UI_BASE_URL=https://argo.example.com
# CLAWQL_WORKFLOW_ALLOW_DELETE=0
# CLAWQL_WORKFLOW_WAIT_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=600
# CLAWQL_WORKFLOW_WAIT_POLL_SECONDS=5
# CLAWQL_WORKFLOW_NOTIFY_ON_TERMINAL=0
# CLAWQL_WORKFLOW_NOTIFY_CHANNEL=C01234567
# CLAWQL_VAULT_DIGEST_HOURS=24

# NATS JetStream workflow + document events (#127 / #254) — requires nats.enabled=true in Helm or external NATS
# CLAWQL_NATS_URL=nats://localhost:4222
# CLAWQL_NATS_JETSTREAM=1
# CLAWQL_NATS_ENABLE_PUBLISH=1
# CLAWQL_NATS_ENABLE_CONSUMER=1
# CLAWQL_NATS_CONSUMER_RESUME_WORKFLOW=1
# CLAWQL_NATS_CONSUMER_IDP_PIPELINE=1          # Nextcloud inbox → run_idp_pipeline
# CLAWQL_NATS_CONSUMER_CONESHARE_FOLLOWUP=1    # Coneshare viewer → resume + notify
# CLAWQL_NATS_CONSUMER_IDP_DURABLE=clawql-idp-pipeline
# CLAWQL_NATS_CONSUMER_CONESHARE_DURABLE=clawql-coneshare-followup
# IDP agent bridge (#128) — Hermes/Pi-friendly; npm run nats:agent-bridge or Helm nats.agentBridge.enabled
# CLAWQL_NATS_AGENT_BRIDGE=1
# CLAWQL_NATS_AGENT_BRIDGE_DURABLE=clawql-idp-agent-bridge
# CLAWQL_MCP_HTTP_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8080/mcp
# CLAWQL_NATS_AGENT_BRIDGE_NOTIFY_CHANNEL=C01234567
# Standalone worker: npm run nats:worker — or Helm nats.worker.enabled + nats.keda.enabled (#257)
# CLAWQL_NATS_SUBJECT_WORKFLOW=clawql.workflow
# CLAWQL_NATS_SUBJECT_DOCUMENT=clawql.document
# CLAWQL_HITL_WEBHOOK_RESUME_WORKFLOW=1   # sync webhook resume (pairs with NATS consumer)

# HITL Label Studio bridge (issue #228) — hitl_enqueue_label_studio + POST /hitl/label-studio/webhook
# CLAWQL_ENABLE_HITL_LABEL_STUDIO=1
# CLAWQL_LABEL_STUDIO_URL=https://label-studio.example.com
# CLAWQL_LABEL_STUDIO_API_TOKEN=...
# CLAWQL_HITL_WEBHOOK_TOKEN=...   # Bearer or X-Clawql-Hitl-Token; required for webhook when NODE_ENV=production

# Onyx knowledge_search_onyx tool (issue #118) — requires bundled `onyx` in the loaded merge + ONYX_BASE_URL + ONYX_API_TOKEN
# CLAWQL_ENABLE_ONYX=1
# Vitest stdio: avoid real Onyx HTTP when CLAWQL_TEST_ONYX_FETCH_STUB=1; optional CLAWQL_TEST_ONYX_FETCH_BODY (JSON text), CLAWQL_TEST_ONYX_FETCH_HTTP_OK=0
# CLAWQL_TEST_ONYX_FETCH_STUB=1

# clawql-ouroboros MCP tools (issues #141 / #142): create seed, run loop, lineage status. Without Postgres URL the event store is in-memory only.
# CLAWQL_ENABLE_OUROBOROS=1
# CLAWQL_OUROBOROS_DATABASE_URL=postgres://user:pass@host:5432/dbname
# Alternative to URL (useful with k8s Secret refs):
# CLAWQL_OUROBOROS_DB_HOST=clawql-mcp-http-ouroboros-postgres
# CLAWQL_OUROBOROS_DB_PORT=5432
# CLAWQL_OUROBOROS_DB_USER=clawql
# CLAWQL_OUROBOROS_DB_PASSWORD=...
# CLAWQL_OUROBOROS_DB_NAME=clawql_ouroboros

# Langfuse eval → Ouroboros seed revision (#250) — POST /observability/langfuse/webhook + ouroboros_propose_seed_revision_from_eval
# CLAWQL_ENABLE_LANGFUSE_EVAL=1   # also requires CLAWQL_ENABLE_OUROBOROS=1
# CLAWQL_LANGFUSE_WEBHOOK_TOKEN=...   # Bearer or X-Langfuse-Webhook-Token; required when NODE_ENV=production
# CLAWQL_LANGFUSE_EVAL_MIN_SCORE=0.8
# CLAWQL_LANGFUSE_EVAL_AUTO_APPLY=0   # set 1 only when you want automatic seed bumps (default dry-run)

# Optional (#120): default Ouroboros executor — after a successful Paperless `execute` step whose JSON body includes a document id, append `onyx::onyx_ingest_document`. Seed must set metadata `onyx_ingest_after_paperless: true`.
# CLAWQL_OUROBOROS_ONYX_AFTER_PAPERLESS=1
# Optional Onyx ingestion API connector credential pair id (integer):
# CLAWQL_ONYX_CC_PAIR_ID=123

# memory_recall (keyword + wikilink graph; optional overrides)
# CLAWQL_MEMORY_RECALL_SCAN_ROOT=Memory
# CLAWQL_MEMORY_RECALL_LIMIT=10
# CLAWQL_MEMORY_RECALL_MAX_DEPTH=2
# CLAWQL_MEMORY_RECALL_MIN_SCORE=1
# CLAWQL_MEMORY_RECALL_MAX_FILES=2000
# CLAWQL_MEMORY_RECALL_SNIPPET_CHARS=520

# Auto _INDEX_{Provider}.md under the recall scan root after successful memory_ingest (issue #38)
# CLAWQL_MEMORY_INDEX_PAGE=0
# CLAWQL_MEMORY_INDEX_PROVIDER=ClawQL
# OKF Memory/index.md (default on with index pages); set 0 to keep only _INDEX_*
# CLAWQL_MEMORY_OKF_INDEX=0
# OKF Memory/log.md append (default on); set 0 to disable
# CLAWQL_MEMORY_OKF_LOG=0

# Hybrid memory index (issue #27): SQLite under the vault unless CLAWQL_MEMORY_DB_PATH is absolute.
# CLAWQL_MEMORY_DB=0                    # disable DB sync + recall graph merge
# CLAWQL_MEMORY_DB_PATH=memory.db
# CLAWQL_MEMORY_DB_SYNC_ON_RECALL=1     # optional: rewrite DB from every recall scan (heavier)
# CLAWQL_MEMORY_CHUNK_MAX_CHARS=2000    # paragraph_v1 hard-split threshold

# Optional semantic index + recall (issues #26 / #28) — tradeoffs: docs/memory/hybrid-memory-backends.md
# CLAWQL_VECTOR_BACKEND=sqlite     # vectors in memory.db only (simplest)
# CLAWQL_VECTOR_BACKEND=postgres   # pgvector when CLAWQL_VECTOR_DATABASE_URL is set; else sqlite vectors + warning
# CLAWQL_VECTOR_DATABASE_URL=postgres://user:pass@host:5432/dbname
# CLAWQL_MEMORY_VECTOR_DUAL_WRITE=0   # when using Postgres: vectors in PG only (no BLOBs in memory.db)
# CLAWQL_EMBEDDING_DIMENSION=1536
# CLAWQL_EMBEDDING_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
# CLAWQL_EMBEDDING_MODEL=text-embedding-3-small
# CLAWQL_EMBEDDING_API_KEY=…   # or OPENAI_API_KEY
# CLAWQL_MEMORY_VECTOR_MIN_SIM=0.28
# CLAWQL_MEMORY_VECTOR_SCORE_BOOST=50

# Optional: log memory MCP tool invocations as shapes only (no vault text). See docs/memory/memory-db-hybrid-implementation.md §7.
# CLAWQL_MCP_LOG_TOOLS=1

# Cuckoo filter over indexed chunk ids + Merkle root over documents (issues #25 / #37). See docs/memory/memory-db-hybrid-implementation.md §7.
# CLAWQL_CUCKOO_ENABLED=1
# CLAWQL_CUCKOO_FINGERPRINT_BITS=12
# CLAWQL_CUCKOO_METRICS=1
# CLAWQL_MERKLE_ENABLED=1

# ─── 11. Sandbox (`sandbox_exec`) — default off; CLAWQL_ENABLE_SANDBOX=1 ──
# CLAWQL_ENABLE_SANDBOX=1
# Backend: omit = bridge only. auto = prefer Seatbelt, then Docker CLI, then bridge (when URL+token below).
# CLAWQL_SANDBOX_BACKEND=auto
# CLAWQL_SANDBOX_BACKEND=kata
# CLAWQL_SANDBOX_BACKEND=bridge
# CLAWQL_SANDBOX_BACKEND=cloudflare
# CLAWQL_SANDBOX_BACKEND=macos-seatbelt
# CLAWQL_SANDBOX_BACKEND=docker
# The Sandbox SDK runs in a Worker; MCP calls this bridge over HTTPS.
# Deploy: cloudflare/sandbox-bridge/ — set BRIDGE_SECRET to match the token below.
# CLAWQL_SANDBOX_BRIDGE_URL=https://clawql-sandbox-bridge.your-subdomain.workers.dev
# CLAWQL_CLOUDFLARE_SANDBOX_API_TOKEN=
# CLAWQL_CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=
# CLAWQL_SANDBOX_PERSISTENCE_MODE=session
# CLAWQL_SANDBOX_TIMEOUT_MS=120000
# CLAWQL_SANDBOX_TIMEOUT_MS_MAX=300000
#
# Docker / Podman backend (CLAWQL_SANDBOX_BACKEND=docker|container|orbstack|podman):
# CLAWQL_SANDBOX_DOCKER_BIN=docker
# CLAWQL_SANDBOX_DOCKER_NETWORK=none
# CLAWQL_SANDBOX_DOCKER_IMAGE_PYTHON=python:3.12-alpine
# CLAWQL_SANDBOX_DOCKER_IMAGE_NODE=node:22-alpine
# CLAWQL_SANDBOX_DOCKER_IMAGE_SHELL=alpine:3.21
# Optional extra docker run flags before image name (space-separated): --cpus 1 --memory 512m
# CLAWQL_SANDBOX_DOCKER_RUN_EXTRA=

# Kata Containers backend (recommended in Kubernetes; CLAWQL_SANDBOX_BACKEND=kata or unset in-cluster auto):
# CLAWQL_SANDBOX_KATA_RUNTIME_CLASS=kata-qemu
# CLAWQL_SANDBOX_KATA_NAMESPACE=clawql-sandbox
# CLAWQL_SANDBOX_KATA_SERVICE_ACCOUNT=clawql-mcp
# CLAWQL_SANDBOX_KATA_ENABLED=1
# CLAWQL_SANDBOX_KATA_IMAGE_PYTHON=python:3.12-alpine
# CLAWQL_SANDBOX_KATA_IMAGE_NODE=node:22-alpine
# CLAWQL_SANDBOX_KATA_IMAGE_SHELL=alpine:3.21

# ─── Workflow test toggles ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Multi-provider workflow: default to dry-run (show request details, do not POST).
WORKFLOW_PREVIEW_JIRA_REQUEST=1
# Set to 1 to actually POST Jira issue.
# WORKFLOW_CREATE_JIRA_ISSUE=1

# ─── 12. Dashboard — Agent Chat + OpenClaw bridge (dashboard/ only) ──────
# Agent Chat proxies POST /api/agent/chat → CLAWQL_DASHBOARD_OPENCLAW_CHAT_URL (HTTP JSON: { message, threadId?, threadTitle? } → { reply, attachments?, steps? }).
# Streaming (SSE): POST /api/agent/chat/stream when CLAWQL_DASHBOARD_CHAT_STREAM=1 (default). Bridge: POST /v1/chat/stream.
# OpenClaw is the `openclaw` CLI, not an HTTP server; local dev uses the bridge: `cd dashboard && npm run openclaw:chat-bridge` (default http://127.0.0.1:8787/v1/chat).
# Then run the dashboard with the same URL (this file is loaded by Next when present; or export in the shell).
# CLAWQL_DASHBOARD_OPENCLAW_CHAT_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8787/v1/chat
# CLAWQL_DASHBOARD_CHAT_STREAM=1
# CLAWQL_DASHBOARD_CHAT_ENRICH=1   # bridge maps OpenClaw session clawql__* tools → steps/attachments (set 0 to disable)
# Kubernetes (Rancher / Helm): set **`dashboard.openclawChatUrl`** instead — see **`charts/clawql-mcp/values-rancher.example.yaml`** and **`docs/deployment/helm.md`** (inject **`CLAWQL_DASHBOARD_OPENCLAW_CHAT_URL`** on the dashboard pod).
# Bridge process env (not read by ClawQL MCP — only by scripts/openclaw-chat-bridge.mjs):
# OPENCLAW_CHAT_BRIDGE_PORT=8787
# CLAWQL_OPENCLAW_AGENT_ID=main
# OPENCLAW_AGENT_TIMEOUT_SEC=120
# CLAWQL_OPENCLAW_BIN=openclaw
#
# OpenRouter (OpenClaw + dashboard chat bridge — provider id `openrouter` in OpenClaw 2026.x):
# - API key here is picked up by `npm run openclaw:chat-bridge` via repo-root .env merge (only keys unset in your shell).
# - Or persist in OpenClaw: `openclaw models auth paste-token --provider openrouter` (see docs).
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-v1-…
# Default model (pick any OpenRouter id; multi-segment ids need the `openrouter/` prefix — see OpenClaw models docs):
#   openclaw models set openrouter/<vendor>/<model>
# Example DeepSeek Flash: `openclaw models set openrouter/deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash` (confirm slug with `openclaw models list --all --provider openrouter | grep -i deepseek`).
#
# clawql-inference — preferred: direct BYOK (disintermediates OpenRouter):
#   DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=sk-…          # and/or GROQ_API_KEY, FIREWORKS_API_KEY, TOGETHER_API_KEY,
#                                  # MISTRAL_API_KEY, XAI_API_KEY, GOOGLE_API_KEY, OPENAI_API_KEY, …
#   clawql inference serve --port 8080
#   curl …/v1/chat/completions -d '{"model":"deepseek/deepseek-chat",…}'
#   # Aliases: clawql/cheap-chat → deepseek/deepseek-chat
#
# clawql-inference — optional OpenRouter escape hatch (keep if you prefer that aggregator):
#   OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-…
#   curl …/v1/chat/completions -d '{"model":"openrouter/deepseek/deepseek-chat",…}'
#   # Optional: CLAWQL_OPENROUTER_BASE_URL CLAWQL_OPENROUTER_HTTP_REFERER CLAWQL_OPENROUTER_APP_TITLE
#   # Optional allowlist: CLAWQL_INFERENCE_PROVIDERS=openrouter
#
# OpenClaw model auth is separate from ClawQL execute tokens: `openclaw agent` prefers ~/.openclaw/agents/<id>/agent/auth-profiles.json and env markers.
# OPENAI_API_KEY in this file does not fix OpenClaw until you add an OpenAI profile or change the default model away from `openai/*`.
# If you see "No API key found for provider openai", run `openclaw models set openrouter/…` (with OPENROUTER_API_KEY) or `openclaw models auth add`. Guide: docs/openclaw/using-openclaw-with-clawql.md
